      "content": "Yes, CRC errors on the physical interface combined with CPU spikes on the core router almost certainly point to a physical layer issue like a faulty SFP, damaged fiber, or a shorted cable causing signal degradation. When the link gets corrupted, the router must constantly run checksums or retransmit packets, which directly triggers the CPU spikes you observed. You should immediately check the SFP module for physical damage, run a failure analysis (often found in your device's menu or via proprietary tools), and swap the cable and transceiver. Replacing these components usually resolves the packet loss and returns latency to normal.",
